2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  CLAIM    T0317 continued: the content-rights call, the downloader's selection, and the decrypt step
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  CHANGE   src/suno/MangoLicense.{hpp,cpp}: unwrapContentKey() reads the rights response and unwraps the key under SHA-256 of the token the request carried -- the bearer first, the response's guest token second -- with the clip id as the AAD. The GCM tag decides which one it was; a mismatch is a refusal, never a wrong key.
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  CHANGE   SunoClient::requestContentKey(): POST /api/mango/rights with `{content_params:{content_id,content_type:"clip"}}` through the existing authenticated queue, so the bearer is attached and a 401 is retried the way every other call is.
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  CHANGE   SunoDownloader: selectMedia() picks the encrypted form first (the presence of `encoding` is the marker, as the site's own client has it) and falls back to the plain mp3 form. The extension follows the CONTENT -- an m4a-opus body is written as .m4a, not as a .mp3 with an MP4 inside it -- and resolveDestPath() and defaultDestPathFor() both take the extension, so the transfer, the tagger and the sidecar writers still agree on one path.
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  CHANGE   The media host check reads the registry's Role::MediaOrigin and Role::CloudFront rows instead of naming one host, so the captured progressive distribution is fetchable. It used to be a literal for the streaming origin alone, which is why the encrypted progressive form -- the form every synced clip carries -- was refused before it was ever fetched.
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  CHANGE   The decrypt runs in the finalize worker, streaming the body through CtrStream, and swaps the result in only once it is complete: a crash leaves either the encrypted body or the decrypted one, never half of each. The decrypted bytes are checked for a container magic before the file is put in place -- a wrong key must not leave an .m4a that no player can open.
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  CHANGE   The MP4 branch of tagAudioFile() writes the same custom metadata the MP3 branch does, as freeform atoms.
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  VERIFY   unit_tests -> "[suite] TestSunoDownloader -> 0" and "[suite] TestMangoCrypto -> 0"; ctest --test-dir build-fast/tests -j3 -> 100% tests passed, 0 failed out of 14, 65.78 s.
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  VERIFY   The new test anEncryptedBodyBecomesAudio drives the whole path with no network: the encrypted selection, the key request, the streaming decrypt, and the extension. It asserts the file that lands is the plaintext, byte for byte, under an .m4a name.
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  NOT-VERIFIED  The live path: a real rights response, a real 7 MB body, and the player opening the result in the app. The tests cover the flow with a fake server and a synthetic license; only a run against the server proves the rest. That is the human half and it is one press of Play away.
2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  NOTE     The rights call works with NO credential at all: an anonymous request is answered with a guest token, and the key unwraps under SHA-256 of that token. The client sends the bearer because it has one and the site's own client does the same, but the fallback exists and is what the capture used.
